kernel: mm: reference counts and RSS counters only on LinuxKPI

LinuxKPI's mm_struct is mm_count, mm_users and a lock; there are no VMAs to look up, no
mmap lock API and no per-VMA locks. With cfg(sf_lkpi) `Mm`, `MmWithUser`, `RssCounter`,
`add_rss_counter()` and `rss_counter()` are built (the C side is helpers/mm.c of
m1-lkpi-extras, where the counters are documented no-ops) and `mm::virt`, `mmput_async`,
the mmap read lock and the VMA read lock are compiled out. The Asahi driver uses exactly
the first set (drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/memacct.rs).

